IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ba-depositor`

-- Banking Act 1959 (Cth) -- worked cases from the seat of the depositor: ss 5(1), 5(4)-(7), 16AD, 16AF, 16AG, 16AH, 16AHA,
-- 16AI, 16AIC(3), 69.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case, an APRA publication or the Banking Regulation 2016 (not deposited). Fixtures are generated by scratchpad
-- gen_banking-act-1959_baseline.py; expected results were written by hand from the deposited text.
--
-- The life (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-chloe): c012 (2010-03-20), "A children's savings account, her mother as
-- signatory" -- "Are her deposits protected?". Chloe is 7. The scenario states no balance, bank or interest: the balance of
-- $500 and accrued interest of $2 are ASSUMED; the account is ASSUMED to be in Chloe's name, in Australian dollars, repayable on
-- demand, with an ADI. The failure is hypothetical: the case asks what would happen if her bank failed and were declared.
-- The limit of $250,000 is an INPUT value from the encoding plan; the Banking Regulation 2016 that sets it is not deposited.
-- The cases read the 2026 compilation; whether the 2010 law differed is not answerable from the deposit.

`Chloe's children's savings account (c012)` MEANS Account WITH
    `kept with an ADI` IS TRUE
    `bank must repay the balance on demand or at an agreed time` IS TRUE
    `prescribed by the regulations as a protected account` IS FALSE
    `prescribed by the regulations as not protected` IS FALSE
    `recorded in Australian currency` IS TRUE
    `is a covered financial product that is not an account` IS FALSE
    `net credit balance at the declaration time` IS 500
    `interest accrued but not credited` IS 2
    `clearance adjustment under the regulations` IS 0
    `number of account-holders` IS 1

